\section{Rules}{

With \code{rule = "sample"} (default), a prediction whose probability of
being true is \code{p} in a draw is judged true with probability \code{p}, so no
threshold is involved; this assumes that the predictions of an occasion
are true or false independently, given the calibration. With
\code{rule = "threshold"}, it is judged true when \code{p >= p_min}, as in
\code{\link[=history_draws]{history_draws()}}; this keeps only the predictions the calibration is
nearly sure of and gives fewer detections.
